1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,835
An antibiotic is about to enter a bacterium.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,632
Everything you will see is a real structure.

3
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:10,142
The proteins come from crystallography.

4
00:00:10,142 --> 00:00:12,781
The motion comes from molecular dynamics.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,605
This is a Gram-negative cell.

6
00:00:15,605 --> 00:00:20,105
Two membranes, a thin wall in between, and only a few ways in.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:29,825
Inside the periplasm, two things can be waiting for the drug: an enzyme that destroys it, or the target it came for.

8
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,214
Same drug. Same door. Two fates.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,861
On the left, a cell that carries a beta-lactamase.

10
00:00:36,861 --> 00:00:39,214
On the right, a cell that does not.

11
00:00:39,214 --> 00:00:40,559
Watch them together.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,185
Through the porin. Identical, frame for frame.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,500
Ceftazidime.

14
00:00:45,422 --> 00:00:47,957
A third-generation cephalosporin.

15
00:00:47,957 --> 00:00:50,416
The same molecule on both sides.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
And here they part.

17
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,998
On the left, the enzyme catches it first.

18
00:00:54,998 --> 00:01:00,986
On the right, there is no enzyme, and the drug finds the protein that is building the wall.

19
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,058
Wall synthesis stops.

20
00:01:03,058 --> 00:01:04,243
The wall opens.

21
00:01:04,243 --> 00:01:06,454
The membrane pushes through.

22
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,473
Now the same chemistry, twice.

23
00:01:09,473 --> 00:01:11,698
The beta-lactam ring opens.

24
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,600
In the enzyme, the broken drug is released.

25
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:16,600
Harmless.

26
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:18,593
On the target, it stays bound.

27
00:01:18,593 --> 00:01:20,282
The protein is locked.

28
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:21,596
One cell dies.

29
00:01:21,596 --> 00:01:23,474
The other never noticed.

30
00:01:23,474 --> 00:01:25,900
One enzyme made the difference.

31
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,013
That is what resistance is.

32
00:01:28,013 --> 00:01:29,578
Not a stronger cell.

33
00:01:29,578 --> 00:01:30,987
One extra protein.

34
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,894
Next: how bacteria get that enzyme, and how they share it.

